\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces Stratified window-level vs grouped subject-out accuracies (mean across 3 folds) --- the compact summary that the rest of this section unpacks. The grouped subject-out protocol holds out 16--18 subjects per fold with zero overlap, so it is the stricter subject-generalisation test. The near-original tier --- RP, GASF and GADF --- is preserved under both sampling schemes: all three match the original-signal accuracy on every classifier. MTF is the single decoder that degrades, and it is significantly outranked by RP, GASF and GADF on all six classifiers under both protocols. Absolute accuracies are lower under grouped subject-out validation because the model has not seen any window from the test subjects.}}{33}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:window_vs_subject_out}{{16}{33}{Discussion}{}{}}
